to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}=$ \n{{field-3}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}=$ \n{{field-4}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the function $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is not defined at $x={90}^{∘},\\,{270}^{∘}.$ \n\nFirst, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}=0\n$$\n\nLet's solve each equation separately.\n\n- First, we solve $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0.$ The solutions to this equation for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$  are $x={0}^{∘},\\,{180}^{∘}.$\n\n- Then, we solve $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}=0,$ or equivalently $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}.$ The solutions to this equation for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ are $x={60}^{∘},\\,{240}^{∘}.$\n\nArranging all solutions from both equations in ascending order, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={0}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={60}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={240}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f0f24e0-da03-5fa3-b3dc-bb383068ae15" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing Reciprocal Functions by Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "241154b1-551f-584c-993e-0c47406592ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542732} {:answer/id #uuid "7a33462a-0b5c-5767-aee9-1552a464064f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542964} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2c5b50-3dd5-52c7-8399-36836c7f2379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543058} {:answer/id #uuid "de49b249-9f4d-5d00-80c8-43736c27b25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543206} {:answer/id #uuid "f8241f88-61bc-51f6-a6e0-1e5c1ffbf1a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "241154b1-551f-584c-993e-0c47406592ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542732} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b13f2ce-c29b-57af-9ebe-adda59545e9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59756d3c-3c85-5289-a62f-143fdaa1a9c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-30184" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Note that the function $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ is not defined at the points where $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0.$ On the interval ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ the excluded values are $x={90}^{∘},\\,{270}^{∘}.$ \n\nFirst, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡x(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=0,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1=0\n$$\n\nLet's solve each equation separately.\n\n- First, we solve $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=0.$ Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ so it is never equal to zero. Therefore, this equation has no solutions.\n\n- Then, we solve $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1=0,$ or equivalently, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ The solutions to this equation for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$  are $x={30}^{∘},\\,{150}^{∘}.$\n\nCombining all solutions from both equations, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={30}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={150}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=4\\,500.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110683 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8553da6-42ce-5b77-97c4-7d9e2ee55f85" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation by Rearranging the Equation and Then Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6769fc2-1f99-58cd-b304-39fd1bc85cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6769fc2-1f99-58cd-b304-39fd1bc85cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543077} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a28f71e-2de4-57c1-adc0-73f5c09d376a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51727bef-15f4-56e8-b56b-7273e05fb720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51727bef-15f4-56e8-b56b-7273e05fb720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542861} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0bff5ee-f0bb-5564-95ca-9d1ccf76e9fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a164d99-c5d0-5aca-9c2d-79ffdfb6a7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a164d99-c5d0-5aca-9c2d-79ffdfb6a7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542751} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0b6ab9f-590f-55f8-9d84-51450b9afb62" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543445} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7dfe15a-21a9-5c24-bd6e-8f28beddda63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7dfe15a-21a9-5c24-bd6e-8f28beddda63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543083} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec791608-10e6-5073-b263-73fdaf240d93" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df0bb882-2469-5cab-82f5-df4eee26a54c" :question/math-academy-id "q-337172" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$ \n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,{x}_{3}=$ \n{{field-3}}$,\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Note that the function $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is not defined at the points where $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0.$ In the given interval, the excluded values are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFirst, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1=0\n$$\n\nLet's solve each equation separately.\n\n- First, we solve $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0.$ The solutions to this equation for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $ are $x=-\\pi ,\\,0.$\n\n- Then, we solve $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1=0,$ or equivalently $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=1.$ The solutions to this equation for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $ are $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nTaking into account that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ are excluded values, and arranging all solutions from both equations in ascending order, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\pi ,\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,{x}_{3}=0,\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110683 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8553da6-42ce-5b77-97c4-7d9e2ee55f85" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation by Rearranging the Equation and Then Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "233192cd-d748-5492-83f5-a8ca027c213a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "233192cd-d748-5492-83f5-a8ca027c213a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542731} :answer-field/id #uuid "042639be-7137-5f5e-a238-735f62cbd938" :answ